Now I have a clear understanding of the vulnerability. Let me compare the two functions:

In `ihevcd_sao_ctb` (line 83), the code initializes `au1_avail_luma` and `au1_avail_chroma` to 255:
```c
for(i = 0; i < 8; i++)
{
    au1_avail_luma[i] = 255;
    au1_avail_chroma[i] = 255;
}
```

In `ihevcd_sao_shift_ctb` (line 526), the "Top-left CTB" section (starting around line 830) has:
```c
else // if(2 <= ps_sao->b3_y_type_idx)
{
    ...
    for(i = 0; i < 8; i++)
    {
        au1_avail_luma[i] = 255;  // This IS initialized here
        ...
    }
```

Wait, let me re-read. The `au1_avail_luma` IS initialized to 255 in the `else // if(2 <= ps_sao->b3_y_type_idx)` block. But what about the `au1_avail_chroma`? Let me check:

